  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GeoStationary Fire data for Developing Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Challenges Research Fund (GCRF) supports cutting-edge research to address challenges faced by developing countries. The fund addresses the UN sustainable development goals. It aims to maximise the impact of research and innovation to improve lives and opportunity in the developing world.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will, among other goals, explore the outputs of NERC-funded research related the European Meteosat satellite covering Europe and Africa, and the billions of dollars invested in new ground- and space-based geostationary satellite infrastructure</narrative>
  </description>
